**Plan: add `--json` in `cli.js`, serialize `buildRows()` straight to JSON.**

```js
const USAGE = 'usage: cli.js report [--json]';

function main(argv) {
  const [command, ...flags] = argv;
  if (command !== 'report' || flags.some((f) => f !== '--json')) {
    process.stderr.write(USAGE + '\n');
    return 1;
  }
  const rows = buildRows();
  const out = flags.includes('--json') ? JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2) : toTable(rows);
  process.stdout.write(out + '\n');
  return 0;
}
```

One call for you. The table drops `owner` and `slow` on purpose, per the note in [format.js:3](src/format.js:3). JSON has no width limit, so I would print all six fields.

That means "same data" as `buildRows()`, not as the table. Say the word if you want the four table columns only.
